One multi-tenant Teams bot serving several organizations, each with its own connection and Source, delivered every tenant's activities to every Source. The microsoft_teams_bot Source now takes an optional tenantId (identity and config unchanged when absent, so existing Sources keep matching), acknowledges other tenants' activities, shows the tenant in its view, and consumers can filter by tenantId. on_activity also outputs the invoke name and object value so Adaptive Card submissions are readable. Tests cover two tenant-limited Sources on one App ID plus an unlimited one, channelData-only tenants, consumer tenant filtering and card submission outputs.
